From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: odin3: use PSCI platform-coordinated idle

The AYN Odin 3 does not reliably wake after Linux enters the SM8750
PSCI OSI/genpd retention hierarchy. UFS system suspend completes with
the link in UIC_LINK_OFF_STATE before the hang, and WFI-only suspend
wakes reliably.

Remove the per-CPU PSCI power-domain links for this board. The generic
CPU idle states remain available, so PSCI can use platform-coordinated
mode instead of Linux OSI/genpd coordination.

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/cq8725s-ayn-odin3.dts | 32 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/cq8725s-ayn-odin3.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/cq8725s-ayn-odin3.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/cq8725s-ayn-odin3.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/cq8725s-ayn-odin3.dts
@@ -233,0 +234,32 @@
+
+&cpu0 {
+	/delete-property/ power-domains;
+	/delete-property/ power-domain-names;
+};
+
+&cpu1 {
+	/delete-property/ power-domains;
+	/delete-property/ power-domain-names;
+};
+
+&cpu2 {
+	/delete-property/ power-domains;
+	/delete-property/ power-domain-names;
+};
+
+&cpu3 {
+	/delete-property/ power-domains;
+	/delete-property/ power-domain-names;
+};
+
+&cpu4 {
+	/delete-property/ power-domains;
+	/delete-property/ power-domain-names;
+};
+
+&cpu5 {
+	/delete-property/ power-domains;
+	/delete-property/ power-domain-names;
+};
+
+&cpu6 {
+	/delete-property/ power-domains;
+	/delete-property/ power-domain-names;
+};
+
+&cpu7 {
+	/delete-property/ power-domains;
+	/delete-property/ power-domain-names;
+};
